{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is running a cobbler orchestrator stitch task (#5312) to complete the cmd/sha256sum utility. The task requires implementing four specific features from srd032:\n   - srd032 R3.2: Add `--zero`/`-z` flag for NUL-delimited output lines instead of newline-delimited\n   - srd032 R4.1: Exit 0 on success, exit 1 when any file fails to hash or checksum verification fails\n   - srd032 R4.2: Support `--help` and `--version` flags with standard GNU-style output\n   - srd032 R4.3: Handle file access errors gracefully (print to stderr, continue processing, set non-zero exit)\n\n   Only `cmd/sha256sum/main.go` should be modified. No git commands should be run.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - GNU coreutils sha256sum behavior matching (differential testing against gsha256sum)\n   - pkg/hashutil shared library: `DigestFiles(files []string, cfg HashConfig, binary, tag bool, stdout, stderr io.Writer) int` and `VerifyChecksums`\n   - pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() for SIGPIPE handling\n   - NUL-delimited output (replacing `\\n` with `\\0` in output lines)\n   - GNU-style `--help` and `--version` output format\n   - Exit code conventions: 0 for success, 1 for any failure\n   - The hashutil.DigestFiles already returns an exit code int and handles file errors internally\n   - Design Decision D1: Use os.Exit with hashutil.DigestFiles return value\n   - Design Decision D2: Follow same --help/--version format as cmd/md5sum (GNU standard format)\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **cmd/sha256sum/main.go** (current implementation, to be modified):\n     - Already has: SIGPIPE handler, basic options struct (binary, tag, check, warn, quiet, status), parseArgs/parseLongFlag/parseShortFlags, DigestFiles and VerifyChecksums integration\n     - Missing: --zero/-z flag, --help flag, --version flag\n     - Exit code handling partially exists (DigestFiles return value used in os.Exit, check mode has exitCode tracking)\n     - Full current content (118 lines):\n     ```go\n     // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n     // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     \n     package main\n     \n     import (\n     \t\"crypto/sha256\"\n     \t\"fmt\"\n     \t\"os\"\n     \t\"strings\"\n     \n     \t\"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/hashutil\"\n     \t\"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n     )\n     \n     func main() {\n     \tsys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n     \topts, files := parseArgs(os.Args[1:])\n     \tcfg := hashutil.HashConfig{\n     \t\tAlgorithm: \"SHA256\",\n     \t\tNewHash:   sha256.New,\n     \t\tDigestLen: 32,\n     \t}\n     \tif opts.check {\n     \t\tcheckOpts := hashutil.CheckOptions{\n     \t\t\tWarn:   opts.warn,\n     \t\t\tQuiet:  opts.quiet,\n     \t\t\tStatus: opts.status,\n     \t\t}\n     \t\texitCode := 0\n     \t\tfor _, f := range files {\n     \t\t\tok, err := hashutil.VerifyChecksums(f, cfg, checkOpts, os.Stdout, os.Stderr)\n     \t\t\tif err != nil {\n     \t\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"sha256sum: %s\\n\", err)\n     \t\t\t\texitCode = 1\n     \t\t\t} else if !ok {\n     \t\t\t\texitCode = 1\n     \t\t\t}\n     \t\t}\n     \t\tos.Exit(exitCode)\n     \t}\n     \tos.Exit(hashutil.DigestFiles(files, cfg, opts.binary, opts.tag, os.Stdout, os.Stderr))\n     }\n     \n     type options struct {\n     \tbinary bool\n     \ttag    bool\n     \tcheck  bool\n     \twarn   bool\n     \tquiet  bool\n     \tstatus bool\n     }\n     \n     func parseArgs(args []string) (options, []string) {\n     \tvar opts options\n     \tvar files []string\n     \ti := 0\n     \tfor i < len(args) {\n     \t\targ := args[i]\n     \t\tif arg == \"--\" {\n     \t\t\tfiles = append(files, args[i+1:]...)\n     \t\t\tbreak\n     \t\t}\n     \t\tif handled, advance := parseLongFlag(arg, &opts); handled {\n     \t\t\ti += advance\n     \t\t\tcontinue\n     \t\t}\n     \t\tif arg == \"-\" || !strings.HasPrefix(arg, \"-\") {\n     \t\t\tfiles = append(files, arg)\n     \t\t\ti++\n     \t\t\tcontinue\n     \t\t}\n     \t\ti += parseShortFlags(arg[1:], &opts)\n     \t}\n     \treturn opts, files\n     }\n     \n     func parseLongFlag(arg string, opts *options) (bool, int) {\n     \tif !strings.HasPrefix(arg, \"--\") {\n     \t\treturn false, 0\n     \t}\n     \tswitch arg {\n     \tcase \"--binary\":\n     \t\topts.binary = true\n     \tcase \"--text\":\n     \t\topts.binary = false\n     \tcase \"--tag\":\n     \t\topts.tag = true\n     \tcase \"--check\":\n     \t\topts.check = true\n     \tcase \"--warn\":\n     \t\topts.warn = true\n     \tcase \"--quiet\":\n     \t\topts.quiet = true\n     \tcase \"--status\":\n     \t\topts.status = true\n     \tdefault:\n     \t\treturn false, 0\n     \t}\n     \treturn true, 1\n     }\n     \n     func parseShortFlags(flags string, opts *options) int {\n     \tfor _, ch := range flags {\n     \t\tswitch ch {\n     \t\tcase 'b':\n     \t\t\topts.binary = true\n     \t\tcase 't':\n     \t\t\topts.binary = false\n     \t\tcase 'c':\n     \t\t\topts.check = true\n     \t\tcase 'w':\n     \t\t\topts.warn = true\n     \t\t}\n     \t}\n     \treturn 1\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - **cmd/md5sum/main.go** (reference pattern, read-only):\n     - Nearly identical structure to sha256sum - same options struct, same parseArgs pattern\n     - Also does NOT have --help, --version, or --zero implemented\n     - Uses `md5.New` with DigestLen 16, Algorithm \"MD5\"\n     - Confirms the pattern: D2 says \"follow same format as cmd/md5sum\" for help/version but md5sum doesn't have them yet, so GNU standard format should be used\n\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd032-sha256sum.yaml** (SRD, read-only):\n     - R1: Digest computation (R1.1-R1.4) - hash format, stdin, --tag, exit on error\n     - R2: Checksum verification (R2.1-R2.3) - --check, OK/FAILED output, --warn/--quiet/--status\n     - R3: Binary/text mode (R3.1-R3.2) - -b/-t flags, --tag overrides\n     - R4: Exit codes and SIGPIPE (R4.1-R4.3) - exit 0/1, SIGPIPE handling\n     - Note: SRD does NOT mention --zero/-z or --help/--version explicitly; these come from the task's requirements mapping\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. Only file reads were performed before the summary was requested.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Key design challenge: The `--zero` flag needs to replace newline terminators with NUL bytes in output. Since `hashutil.DigestFiles` writes directly to the provided `io.Writer` (stdout), the solution is to wrap `os.Stdout` with a custom writer that replaces `\\n` with `\\0` when `--zero` is active. This avoids modifying the shared `pkg/hashutil` package.\n   - For `--help` and `--version`: These should be handled early in main() before any file processing. They print to stdout and exit 0 immediately.\n   - Exit code handling is mostly already correct via `hashutil.DigestFiles` return value and the check-mode loop.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: Extremely long task description containing the full project context (CLAUDE.md, ARCHITECTURE, VISION, SRDs, roadmap, requirement states, execution constitution, go style constitution, task description with requirements/design decisions/acceptance criteria/constraints). The task is to implement srd032 R3.2, R4.1, R4.2, R4.3 in cmd/sha256sum/main.go.\n   - Second message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - requesting a detailed summary of the conversation.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Modify `cmd/sha256sum/main.go` to add:\n     1. `zero` field to options struct + `--zero`/`-z` flag parsing\n     2. `help` and `version` fields + `--help`/`--version` flag parsing  \n     3. Handle --help early in main() → print usage to stdout, exit 0\n     4. Handle --version early in main() → print version to stdout, exit 0\n     5. When `zero` is true, wrap stdout with a NUL-replacing writer before passing to DigestFiles/VerifyChecksums\n   - Run `go build -o bin/sha256sum ./cmd/sha256sum/` and `go vet ./cmd/sha256sum/` to verify\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/sha256sum/... -count=1` to verify tests pass\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading all three required files (sha256sum/main.go, md5sum/main.go, srd032-sha256sum.yaml) and was about to begin implementing the changes to cmd/sha256sum/main.go when the summary was requested. No code changes have been made yet. The implementation plan was formed:\n   \n   - Add `zero`, `help`, `version` bool fields to the `options` struct\n   - Add `--zero`, `--help`, `--version` to `parseLongFlag` switch cases\n   - Add `z` to `parseShortFlags` switch cases\n   - In main(), after parseArgs, check opts.help → print usage, exit 0; check opts.version → print version, exit 0\n   - Create a `nulWriter` type that wraps an `io.Writer` and replaces `\\n` with `\\0`\n   - When opts.zero is true, wrap os.Stdout with nulWriter before passing to DigestFiles or VerifyChecksums\n   - Ensure all acceptance criteria (AC1-AC5) are met\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write the modified `cmd/sha256sum/main.go` with all the changes described above, then run `go build -o bin/sha256sum ./cmd/sha256sum/` and `go vet ./cmd/sha256sum/` to verify compilation, followed by `go test ./cmd/sha256sum/... -count=1`.\n\n   The task description states: \"Implement srd032 R3.2 -- add --zero/-z flag for NUL-delimited output lines instead of newline-delimited\", \"Implement srd032 R4.2 -- support --help and --version flags with standard GNU-style output\", \"Implement srd032 R4.1 -- exit 0 on success, exit 1 when any file fails to hash or any checksum verification fails\", and \"Implement srd032 R4.3 -- handle file access errors gracefully: print error to stderr, continue processing remaining files, and set non-zero exit code\".\n\nIf you need 