{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0198ncVK2T48QnCxWi7WDSZB","type":"tool_result","content":"/opt/homebrew/bin/gsha256sum\nUsage: gsha256sum [OPTION]... [FILE]...\nPrint or check SHA256 (256-bit) checksums.\nLegacy interface to the cksum utility.\n\nWith no FILE, or when FILE is -, read standard input.\n  \u001b]8;;https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#cksum-b\u001b\\\u001b[1m-b, --binary\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u001b\\\n         read in binary mode\n  \u001b]8;;https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#cksum-c\u001b\\\u001b[1m-c, --check\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u001b\\\n         read checksums from the FILEs and check them\n      \u001b]8;;https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#cksum--tag\u001b\\\u001b[1m--tag\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u001b\\\n         create a BSD-style checksum\n  \u001b]8;;https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#cksum-t\u001b\\\u001b[1m-t, --text\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u001b\\\n         read in text mode (default)\n  \u001b]8;;https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#cksum-z\u001b\\\u001b[1m-z, --zero\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u001b\\\n         end each output line with NUL, not newline,\n         and disable file name escaping\n\nThe following five options are useful only when verifying checksums:\n      \u001b]8;;https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#cksum--ignore-missing\u001b\\\u001b[1m--ignore-missing\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u001b\\\n         don't fail or report status for missing files\n      \u001b]8;;https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#cksum--quiet\u001b\\\u001b[1m--quiet\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u001b\\\n         don't print OK for each successfully verified file\n      \u001b]8;;https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#cksum--status\u001b\\\u001b[1m--status\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u001b\\\n         don't output anything, status code shows success\n      \u001b]8;;https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#cksum--strict\u001b\\\u001b[1m--strict\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u001b\\\n         exit non-zero for improperly formatted checksum lines\n  \u001b]8;;https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#cksum-w\u001b\\\u001b[1m-w, --warn\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u001b\\\n         warn about improperly formatted checksum lines\n      \u001b]8;;https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/cksum#cksum--help\u001b\\\u001b[1m--help\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u001b\\\n         display this help and exit\n      \u001b]8;;https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/cksum#cksum--version\u001b\\\u001b[1m--version\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u001b\\\n         output version information and exit\n\nThe sums are computed as described in FIPS-180-2.\nWhen checking, the input should be a former output of this program.\nThe default mode is to print a line with: checksum, a space,\na character indicating input mode ('*' for binary, ' ' for text\nor where binary is insignificant), and name for each FILE.\n\nThere is no difference between binary mode and text mode on GNU systems.\n\nReport bugs to: bug-coreutils@gnu.org\nGNU coreutils home page: <https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/>\nGeneral help using GNU software: <https://www.gnu.org/gethelp/>\nFull documentation <https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/sha256sum>\nor available locally via: info '(coreutils) sha2 utilities'","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4a29dd0e-05c2-41ac-b24f-7283ae52b9aa","uuid":"89521835-483f-44be-9945-42284e956c85","timestamp":"2026-05-19T23:25:28.660Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"/opt/homebrew/bin/gsha256sum\nUsage: gsha256sum [OPTION]... [FILE]...\nPrint or check SHA256 (256-bit) checksums.\nLegacy interface to the cksum utility.\n\nWith no FILE, or when FILE is -, read standard input.\n  \u001b]8;;https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#cksum-b\u001b\\\u001b[1m-b, --binary\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u001b\\\n         read in binary mode\n 